WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.420
Your pricing strategy, your value story, and your next 90 days.

2
00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.910
This is the video for Module 4 of Pricing and Value Strategy.

3
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:19.320
You have built separate pieces through this course. A pricing strategy puts them on one or two pages, so you can quote quickly and explain every number.

4
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.790
Start with your cost floor, and the date you calculated it.

5
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.580
Add your market range and where you sit in it.

6
00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:40.070
List your models and packages, with a short reason beside each price. For example, Zainab's Standard is about 22% above her floor and inside the market range.

7
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:51.730
Then your scope and change prices, payment terms, discount policy, and when you will next review. Save it on your phone, so you can quote in minutes during a WhatsApp chat.

8
00:00:52.980 --> 00:01:00.590
The method works for any service. Funmi manages email, calendars and customer messages for small business owners.

9
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.900
She needs 180,000 naira a month in personal pay.

10
00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.600
Her business costs are 60,000 naira.

11
00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.330
She adds a 10% buffer of 24,000 naira.

12
00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:19.270
Her monthly target is 264,000 naira.

13
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:27.300
She can work 140 hours a month, and about 60% is billable. That is 84 hours.

14
00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:37.360
264,000 divided by 84, rounded up, gives a minimum rate of 3,150 naira an hour.

15
00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:48.280
Her Inbox and Calendar package takes about 10 hours. Its floor is 31,500 naira, and she prices it at 38,000.

16
00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:57.530
Business Admin takes about 20 hours. Its floor is 63,000 naira, and she prices it at 75,000.

17
00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:08.120
Extra hours cost 3,500 naira each, agreed in writing before the work starts. She can explain every number in one sentence.

18
00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:16.860
A client does not buy '16 posts a month'. She buys more enquiries, less stress, and a page that looks professional.

19
00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:30.570
So lead with the value, then list the features that deliver it. Back it with real results, always with the client's permission. Never exaggerate or invent results. Clients talk to each other.

20
00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:38.470
For example, a new catering client asks Zainab for her price. First, she restates the client's goal.

21
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:49.260
Then she shares evidence, with permission. For another caterer, WhatsApp enquiries went from about 15 to about 25 a week over three months.

22
00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:54.990
Then she presents her three packages, each with one line on what it achieves.

23
00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:06.540
She frames Standard in the client's terms. 70,000 naira is about 2,333 naira a day, roughly the profit from 6 extra orders.

24
00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:13.410
Then she stops. The client chooses Standard. No discount, and no promise she cannot keep.

25
00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:22.380
If you start with the price, the client judges it against nothing. Start with her goal, and she judges it against what she wants to gain.

26
00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:31.540
New prices only matter once clients pay them. In week 1, Zainab finalises her strategy and a dated rate card.

27
00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:39.580
In week 2, she gives Client D 30 days' notice of a move from 40,000 to 58,000 naira.

28
00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.620
Then she quotes at least 8 qualified enquiries.

29
00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:56.090
At week 8 she checks her numbers. Her decision rule: if she wins at least 5 of 8 quotes with no price objections, Standard rises to 75,000 naira next quarter.

30
00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:05.130
And if a below-floor client leaves, those freed hours can earn more with a new client. Your buffer carries you through a slow month.

31
00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:15.640
Now assemble your strategy, design your rate card, and write your 90-day plan. The first time you hold a price calmly, write it in your log.

32
00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.930
Continue with the lessons below.
